---
description: Semantic and accessible HTML rules (handbook Day 2)
globs: "**/*.html"
alwaysApply: false
---
- Landmarks: one <header>, <nav> for navigation, one <main id="main-content">, <footer>.
  Include a "Skip to content" link as the first focusable element.
- Exactly one <h1> (the hero headline). Never skip heading levels. Choose levels by
  structure, never by font size.
- Links (<a href>) navigate; buttons (<button type="button">) act. Wishlist, search
  toggle, menu toggle and carousel controls are buttons. Product names are links.
- Every <img> has alt: describe purpose for meaningful images, alt="" for decorative ones.
- Mobile/desktop image pairs use <picture> with <source media="(min-width: …)">.
  Add width/height attributes to reduce layout shift; loading="lazy" below the fold only.
- Videos: <video autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="…">.
- Each product card is an <article>. Lists of links are <ul>/<li>.
- Forms: every input has an associated <label> (visually-hidden is fine); placeholder
  is never a label; email input uses type="email", name, and autocomplete="email".
- div/span only when no semantic element fits. Icon-only buttons need an aria-label.
- No ARIA where a native element already does the job.
